---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ComparisonGrid from "../../components/ComparisonGrid.astro";
import { entitiesOfKind } from "../../lib/domain/canonical";
const criteria = entitiesOfKind("criterion");
---
<BaseLayout title="Method" description="How Ends and Means separates questions, proposed institutions, evidence, and judgment." fullBleed>
  <article class="editorial-page method-page"><header class="editorial-header"><p class="coordinate">METHOD</p><h1>Method</h1><p class="dek measure-standfirst">Ends and Means separates what people sought, what institutions were supposed to do, what happened in bounded cases, and how evidence is judged. The method does not score a winner or flatten a country into one system.</p></header>
    <section class="method-sequence" aria-labelledby="sequence-title"><h2 id="sequence-title">How does an argument connect to evidence?</h2><ol><li><strong>Challenge</strong><span>The recurring question being asked</span></li><li><strong>End</strong><span>What a named actor sought</span></li><li><strong>Means</strong><span>The proposed roles, rules, authority, and incentives</span></li><li><strong>Case</strong><span>What operated where, when, and for whom</span></li><li><strong>Outcome</strong><span>A sourced result with stated limits</span></li><li><strong>Criterion</strong><span>The stated assumptions used to judge it</span></li></ol><p>These capitalized terms name distinct parts of the project’s evidence model; keeping them separate prevents a proposal from being mistaken for an observed result.</p></section>
    <section class="criteria-section" aria-labelledby="criteria-title"><header><p class="coordinate">JUDGMENT</p><h2 id="criteria-title">Which assumptions shape a judgment?</h2></header><ComparisonGrid itemCount={criteria.length} className="criteria-grid">{criteria.map((criterion) => <article><h3>{criterion.label}</h3><p>{criterion.definition}</p><dl><div><dt>Assumption</dt><dd>{criterion.normativeAssumptions.join(" ")}</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence needed</dt><dd>{criterion.evidenceRequirements.join(" ")}</dd></div><div><dt>Limit</dt><dd>{criterion.limitations.join(" ")}</dd></div></dl></article>)}</ComparisonGrid></section>
    <section class="model-boundary"><p class="coordinate">LIMITS</p><h2>What happens when evidence is missing?</h2><p>Each claim keeps its sources, exact location, scope, uncertainty, and relationship status. Missing coverage stays blank instead of becoming a conclusion. Specific limitations remain visible in the <a href="/research/">open research questions</a>, where objections, conflicting observations, and causal alternatives remain distinct.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
